Delete and revise Subsection (o) of Section 8.10.2.2.2 to read as follows:

8.10.2.2.2 Machine room.

(o) Braking System. For passenger elevators and all freight elevators, the brake shall be tested for compliance with applicable requirements. A test of the brake shall be made with 125 percent of load. When the car returns to one of the lower landings, the main line switch shall be pulled while the car is running at inspection speed to ensure the brake has set and holds the load. The driving machine shall safely lower, stop, and hold the car with this load. Freight elevators of class C-2 loading shall sustain and level the elevator car. (Section 2.16.6) (Item 2.15 of ASME A17.2).
(1) Braking system (Section 2.24.8.2.2).
(2) Electromechanical brake (Section 2.24.8.3).

