Temporary risers shall be at least 4 inches in (102 mm) diameter for structures less than 450 feet high (137 160 mm) and at least 6 inches (152 mm) in diameter for structures 450 feet (137 160 mm) high or more. There shall be as many risers as will be, or were, required for the permanent system. Each such riser shall be connected to a cross connection that is supplied through two-way Fire Department hose connections at the street level, and shall be equipped on each floor with a 2½ inch (64 mm) hose outlet valve. The installations shall be made so that each riser, cross connection, and branch line can be plugged or capped when work is not being done on the system.

